# The images this estate runs, as paths under the upstream registry the
# caching repository proxies.
#
# Nothing here is built. Every workload in this repository is somebody else's
# image, which makes where it is pulled from a decision rather than a detail.
#
# Note that one of these publishes to its own hostname, which turns out to be a
# mirror of the common registry rather than a separate one: the rate limit it
# returns names the registry underneath. Indirecting the pull is what makes
# that irrelevant.
#
# The bootstrap resolves each of these through the estate's own repository and
# deploys the digest it gets back, never the tag. A tag is a pointer somebody
# else can move; a digest is the image. ADR 12.
erpnext=frappe/erpnext:v16.34.1
n8n=n8nio/n8n:1.64.3
postgres=library/postgres:16-alpine
vaultwarden=vaultwarden/server:1.32.7
